## Pre-open daily seed capture (P-run) — REPLAY_CONTRACT §12.10.1.
## One oneshot run per trading day, before the market open: it captures the
## ka10099 universe and one ka10081 page per symbol into
## runs/<session_date>-preopen/ and seals it with daily_seed_manifest.
## The same day's session launcher (tools/run_session.sh) discovers that
## committed P-run and starts the collector with --daily-seed.
##
## ExecStart is the server-side wrapper (the hongscanner-session-start.sh
## analog): it calls the repository's tools/run_preopen.sh with the
## operator's --calendar/--profile/--environment arguments. The wrapper is
## installed on the server, not in this repository; the unit is inert
## until it exists.
##
## Type=oneshot: the capture has one finite job and a real exit status
## (0 sealed, 2 refusal, 3 calendar, 4 capture failure). Restart is
## deliberately absent: a failed P-run keeps its unsealed evidence and a
## retry must use a NEW run directory, never overwrite the failure.
##
## TimeoutStartSec covers a slow vendor: ~2,600 one-page requests plus the
## market chains; the run itself fails closed at the calendar open.
[Unit]
Description=Hong Scanner Pre-open Daily Seed Capture (P-run)

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=/home/wintrover/hongscanner
ExecStart=/home/wintrover/.local/bin/hongscanner-preopen-start.sh
Environment=PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1
TimeoutStartSec=30min